<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#SharedEvaluationContext> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Two candidate models evaluated on the same SharedEvaluationContext (identical it6:Task, dcat:Dataset, daimo:datasetVersion, daimo:protocol, and — when the procedure is stochastic — the same daimo:randomSeed) can be ranked on the same metric; changing task, dataset, version or protocol, or comparing under incompatible metrics, breaks comparability. A deterministic protocol such as leave-one-out may omit the seed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "daimo" .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ParticipantRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dataspace-scoped role played by a participant with respect to AI assets (anti-rigid; an agent gains and loses roles over time)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#offersModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://data.europa.eu/it6/MachineLearningModel> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelConsumer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Role of an agent that discovers, negotiates, and invokes AI models offered by a Model Provider."@en .
