_:ne83e70ac7f56477da30889730e5f818db9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#AuditEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#offeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ParticipantRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelConsumer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ParticipantRole> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ExecutionAuthorization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A governance artefact that binds an accepted odrl:Agreement (via daimo:derivedFromAgreement) to the concrete MLDCAT-AP run invocations it authorises (daimo:authorizesRun), for a specific grantee agent (daimo:grantedTo) and until an expiry timestamp (daimo:expiresAt). The authorization is NOT the agreement itself: it is a separate individual that operationalises a single agreement over one or more executions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#randomSeed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fixes stochastic components of the evaluation procedure when that procedure uses them. Functional: a given SharedEvaluationContext must not declare two incompatible seeds. Optional: SHACL allows cardinality 0..1 because applicability depends on the evaluation procedure, not on a universal DAIMO list of 'stochastic protocols'. Omitting the seed is not a claim of complete reproducibility; it only records that the declared protocol does not use a seed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasOfferPolicy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has offer policy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#grantedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ExecutionAuthorization> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasAuditEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#evidenceOf> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#contextFlow> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#contextDataset> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The dcat:Dataset the evaluation context is defined over. Functional. Not declared a subproperty of it6:trainedOn because an evaluation-context dataset is an evaluation dataset, not necessarily a training dataset."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ParticipantRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "participant role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#forService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links an I/O contract to the specific dcat:DataService endpoint it applies to. Functional: each contract describes exactly one service (several contracts may still describe the same service if a real need arises, e.g. distinct authentication variants, but a single contract targets one service). Asymmetric: a contract and the service it describes are distinct individuals. Introduced to remove the ambiguity that appears when a ModelDeployment exposes several services (daimo:exposedAs) and declares several contracts (daimo:hasIOContract) with no per-endpoint link, which otherwise forces CQ-R4/CQ-D3/CQ-E1/CQ-G2 into a cartesian join between services and contracts. No external property (e.g. dcat:endpointDescription) carries this exact meaning; see alignment.ttl for the non-alignment rationale."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#SharedEvaluationContext> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reified grouping of the conditions under which model evaluations are comparable: task, dataset, dataset version, evaluation protocol and, when applicable, random seed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelProvider> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "model provider"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#grantedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#outputFormat> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#inputSchema> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "input schema"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasIOContract> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelDeployment> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#AIAssetOffering> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A catalog-record entry registering an AI model in a dataspace catalog as a governed offer, bundling the model, the issuing agent, and an ODRL offer policy."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasOffering> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#offersModel> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#expiresAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#outputFormat> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#offersModel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "DAIMO is an integration profile that connects DCAT-AP, MLDCAT-AP, ODRL, PROV-O, and the Dataspace Protocol (DSP, as operationalised by Eclipse EDC) to support publication, discovery, invocation, execution traceability, and contextualised evaluation of AI model assets exchanged in dataspaces. The edc: namespace is used only for EDC-specific extensions (e.g., ParticipantContext) not yet standardised in DSP."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "0.1.7" .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasOffering> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://data.europa.eu/it6/MachineLearningModel> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#grantedTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#AuditEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A compliance-oriented evidence record attached to a governed activity, carrying a structured SPDX checksum (algorithm + digest), a signer, and a timestamp."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#deploysModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a deployment to the model it serves. Functional: one deployment serves one model. Asymmetric: a deployment and its model are distinct individuals."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#AuditEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#onInfrastructure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a deployment to the MLDCAT-AP computer infrastructure running it. Functional: one deployment runs on one canonical infrastructure instance (redundancy is modelled as multiple deployments)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#authorizedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#authorizesRun> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo/docs> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#contextDataset> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "context dataset"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#randomSeed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> .
_:ne83e70ac7f56477da30889730e5f818db5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:ne83e70ac7f56477da30889730e5f818db6 .
