<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasAuditEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has audit evidence"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#forService> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "On a deployment exposing a REST endpoint and a gRPC endpoint, the REST IOContract (application/json, oauth2-bearer) declares daimo:forService the REST dcat:DataService and the gRPC IOContract (application/x-protobuf, mtls) declares daimo:forService the gRPC dcat:DataService, so each endpoint's format and authentication method are unambiguous."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#signedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Functional: one signer per evidence record."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#IOContract> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The minimum machine-actionable invocation contract for a deployment: the service it applies to (daimo:forService), input format, output format, authentication method, and optional input/output schemas. Binding each contract to exactly one dcat:DataService is what lets a multi-endpoint deployment expose, e.g., a JSON/OAuth2 REST service and a protobuf/mTLS gRPC service without ambiguity."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#CrossParticipantProvenanceRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasDerivedArtifact> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inverse of daimo:derivedFromRun: from a run, retrieve every derived artifact it produced. Non-functional (a run may produce multiple governed outputs)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#forService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#IOContract> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#evidenceOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AsymmetricProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#exposedAs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#DataService> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelProvider> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Role of an agent that publishes one or more AI models as governed offerings in a dataspace catalog."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ExecutionAuthorization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A governed authorisation resource (a prov:Entity) that links exactly one accepted odrl:Agreement (daimo:derivedFromAgreement) to the it6:Run invocations it permits. Deliberately NOT a subclass of odrl:Agreement: the agreement is the negotiated policy artefact that carries the ODRL permissions, whereas the authorization is the derived resource that ties that agreement to concrete executions, a grantee, and an expiry. Keeping them apart lets one agreement back several authorizations and prevents the authorization from being (mis)typed as an odrl:Policy. SHACL invariant INV-9 checks that the grantee (daimo:grantedTo) is the odrl:assignee of the agreement it derives from."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#derivedFromRun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "derived from run"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#derivedFromAgreement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#priorVersion> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo/0.1.6> .
_:ne83e70ac7f56477da30889730e5f818db7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ExecutionAuthorization> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#PlatformOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Role of an agent responsible for operating the dataspace runtime, hosting model deployments, and enforcing policy at runtime."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#IOContract> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A REST inference endpoint might declare an IOContract with inputFormat \"application/json\", outputFormat \"application/geo+json\", and authMethod \"oauth2-bearer\"; a parallel gRPC endpoint on the same deployment can declare a second IOContract with inputFormat \"application/x-protobuf\" and authMethod \"mtls\"."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasOffering> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has offering"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#derivedFromAgreement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#signedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#onInfrastructure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelDeployment> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#PlatformOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Role of an agent responsible for operating the dataspace runtime, hosting model deployments, and enforcing policy."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasOffering> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/isPrimaryTopicOf> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#AIAssetOffering> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelProvider> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ParticipantRole> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#contextTask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://data.europa.eu/it6/hasTask> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#TopLevelKindsDisjointness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Asserts that the nine top-level DAIMO-native kinds are pairwise disjoint. ParticipantRole subclasses are deliberately excluded so that a single agent may simultaneously hold several roles (e.g., a research group acting as both Evaluator and Model Provider)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasOfferPolicy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/hasPolicy> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#authMethod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#GovernanceActor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Role of an agent that audits execution evidence, enforces compliance obligations, and validates governance across the dataspace."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ExecutionAuthorization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#forService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#DataService> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo/0.1.7> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ParticipantRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An agent acting as a Model Provider within a given EDC participant context has a ParticipantRole instance of type ModelProvider connected via daimo:hasRole and scoped by daimo:inParticipantContext."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#signedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "signed by"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ExecutionAuthorization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#derivedFromAgreement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#usesEvaluationContext> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://data.europa.eu/it6/Evaluation> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelProvider> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Any organisation that declares one or more AIAssetOfferings under its own authorship and policy holds a ModelProvider role in the dataspace contexts where those offerings are listed."@en .
