<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#offeredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links an offering to the agent that authored the offered AI model (i.e., the model provider). Functional: each offering has exactly one offering agent. Deliberately NOT declared rdfs:subPropertyOf dct:publisher: on a dcat:CatalogRecord, dct:publisher denotes the catalog maintainer (the platform registering the record), not the author of the asset being registered. Conflating them would entail that the catalog-time publisher is the model creator — semantically wrong in a real dataspace where e.g. INESData publishes records authored by UPM."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#CrossParticipantProvenanceRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasAuditEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#AuditEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#derivedFromAgreement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a daimo:ExecutionAuthorization to the single accepted odrl:Agreement whose terms it enforces over concrete runs. Functional: each authorization derives from exactly one agreement (a run's authorisation must trace to one accepted set of terms). Asymmetric: the authorization and the agreement are distinct individuals. Deliberately NOT declared a subproperty of prov:wasDerivedFrom: prov:wasDerivedFrom has domain and range prov:Entity and expresses generic data-lineage between entities; using it would (i) force every odrl:Agreement to be a prov:Entity, and (ii) blur the specific governance meaning 'the accepted ODRL agreement this authorization enforces'. No property in ODRL, DCAT, MLDCAT-AP, PROV-O or DSP carries this exact meaning, so daimo:derivedFromAgreement is a native, unaligned object property; see alignment.ttl for the non-alignment rationale."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#derivedFromAgreement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ExecutionAuthorization> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#protocol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#records> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelDeployment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A PlatformOperator that stands up a live inference endpoint for a given model creates a ModelDeployment that (i) deploys the model, (ii) is exposed as one or more dcat:DataServices (e.g., REST + gRPC), (iii) runs on a specific it6:ComputerInfrastructure, and (iv) declares an IOContract per exposed service."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#contextFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://data.europa.eu/it6/Flow> .
