<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#SharedEvaluationContext> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A reified grouping of the conditions under which model results are comparable: task, dataset, dataset version, protocol and, when applicable, random seed. Does not claim that those facets alone guarantee comparability (the same metric and compatible conditions are also required), nor that every facet of a study is covered (split strategy, hyperparameters, metric formula). Absence of a seed is not an assertion of complete reproducibility; it records that the declared procedure does not use one. This is the minimum grouping required by CQ-V1..CQ-V3."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#grantedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "granted to"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#derivedFromRun> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AsymmetricProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#ModelProvider> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Role of an agent that publishes AI models as governed offerings in a dataspace catalog."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#AIAssetOffering> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A catalog-record entry that registers an AI model in a dataspace catalog, bundling the model reference, the providing agent, and an ODRL offer policy. Specialises dcat:CatalogRecord; carries an odrl:Offer via daimo:hasOfferPolicy. In DSP terms this is the catalog-time artefact that becomes a dspace:ContractOffer during negotiation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pionera/daimo#hasDerivedArtifact> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://data.europa.eu/it6/Run> .
